## Decision proposed

Replace subject-only merging in [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) with evidence-based triage. Preserve that accepted decision as history. This proposal has not been accepted by the support desk.

The [incident article](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one queued fix. Its computed view contradicts that narrative: a shared parser problem and a booking-form hint problem are filed together. Two fixes must be tracked separately. Classification is a routing inference, not a reproduced production diagnosis.

## What the current components show

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The parser reads month first for day-first tenants. The hint path applies to form reports from day-first tenants using booking-v3: its MM/DD/YYYY hint conflicts with interpretation in tenant order. App and email reports from those same tenants still take the parser path. Use tenant configuration; a reporter's browser locale and intake tag are not authoritative.

## Evidence review and accounting

<ReviewFindings />

Count a report ID once, even if export pages overlap. Keep the computed filing count separate from the number of customer descriptions that directly support it. Both proposed issues retain their full filing counts with explicit caveats; no uncertain report is silently dropped or counted twice.

R-41203 describes 2 December becoming 12 February and supports a transposition. R-41230 describes 6 January versus 1 June, but copper.studio's booking-v3 form puts it on the hint path. Similar symptoms can have different mechanisms.

### Symptoms not explained by a demonstrated swap

- R-41202: May 12 versus May 11. Obtain intended start time, event timezone and original invite.
- R-41209: one-day errors only in June. Compare affected and unaffected events, including offset handling.
- R-41236: invite allegedly arrived before booking. Obtain creation and delivery logs before inferring an ordering failure.
- R-41344: Lisbon Tuesday versus Toronto Monday for the same meeting. This may be correct local display of one instant; inspect the event timezone and timestamps.
- R-41620: October 6 displayed as Monday. Obtain the full result date and calendar payload.

The tenant-based code files these under parser; that does not establish their actual cause. Timezone conversion across midnight, including incorrect seasonal-offset handling, is a hypothesis from the human review, not a confirmed third bug. None of these records supplies appointment creation time, event start time or timezone payload. Report receipt and merge times cannot replace those fields.

### Reports with too little detail

R-41290 requests a day-first setting. R-41417 reports wrong-day customer impact without dates. R-41514 describes a telephone/words workaround. R-41615 describes October bookings appearing in January without day numbers. Keep them traceable under their filing, but obtain reproductions before attributing a mechanism.

## Why subjects cannot decide duplication

<DedupeExplorer />

The executable examples reject the prose rule in decision 0001. Different subjects can share a cause, while matching subjects can cross causes. Missing tenant configuration means the cause is unknown, not that two unknown reports are duplicates. Inspect tenant, locale, form version, channel and the actual symptom before merging.

## Timing and freshness

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Read received and merged as separate series. A bulk merge is administrative activity, not proof of a simultaneous customer incident. The export is dated 2026-10-04; it is not a live queue. This page's review date records this review, not a refresh of the export. Refresh the data and recheck counts before submission or operational decisions.

## Engineering outcome · 5 October

The [Challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) now reports #4471 closed on 5 October. This update is later than the supplied 4 October export; the historical counts above remain tied to that export.

- Parser: **FIXED**, `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. [Our parser ticket](https://github.com/Ignolek/mega-s01e03/issues/1) is closed as completed, based on the desk's engineering update.
- Hint: **WON'T FIX**, booking-v3 form retired. [Our hint ticket](https://github.com/Ignolek/mega-s01e03/issues/2) is closed as not planned. Retirement removes the affected form; it is not a shipped hint correction.

Closing these tickets records the desk's two different dispositions. It does not prove the cause of the unresolved descriptions, establish the timezone hypothesis, or mean we independently verified production behavior.

## Follow-up and verification

Verify the reported parser fix against ambiguous dates and round trips using explicit tenant order. Verify that booking-v3 has actually been retired and that replacement forms use consistent hints and input interpretation. These are proposed follow-up checks; we have not independently reproduced or deployed either engineering outcome.

Preserve all unresolved report IDs, request original calendar files and timestamps with named zones, and test the human's timezone hypothesis against the evidence. Do not infer a timezone defect merely from different local dates for the same instant.

